  "lessons": "# SCORING LESSONS\n\n- **Indigenous & local community coverage**: Strongly favored\u2014celebrations, governance, reconciliation, education, and Cariboo/BC regional stories. Includes First Nations advocacy, land stewardship, and healing initiatives.\n\n- **Environmental & climate action**: Liked when framed as solutions, scientific discovery, or protection (wildfire response, species preservation, sustainable farming, heat wave science). Rejected when emphasizing crisis/disaster alone or as lifestyle trend.\n\n- **Science & nature discovery**: Favored\u2014unusual phenomena, animal behavior, astronomy, materials science, medical breakthroughs (brain changes, sleep impact, disease detection). Rejects symptom-focused medical advice and wellness pseudoscience.\n\n- **AI: critical analysis over hype**: Accepts nuanced concerns (job impact, deployment speed, trust issues, efficiency problems, legal accountability). Rejects promotional product launches, VC narratives, startup drama, stock/hiring coverage, and speculative fiction treating AI as inevitable savior/threat.\n\n- **Practical tech guides & privacy**: Strong preference for user-empowering how-tos (security, tracking, free features, cross-device solutions, accessible device features). Rejects product reviews, shopping deals, gear optimization, and lifestyle aspirations.\n\n- **Journalism & institutional accountability**: Valued as standalone merit\u2014press freedom, First Nations advocacy, government transparency. Rejects sensationalism, celebrity crime, violent incidents, human-interest tragedy (crashes, deaths), and election/partisan coverage.\n\n- **Geopolitical & conflict reporting**: Consistently rejected\u2014military focus, violence, ceasefire updates, international unrest, protest arrests. Includes UN crises and regional instability.\n\n- **Consumer/lifestyle exclusion zone**: Rejects gear reviews, shopping features, entertainment rankings, fitness optimization, food trends, home d\u00e9cor, relationship advice, and \"try this\" wellness content\u2014even if technically sound.\n\n- **Local governance & civic engagement**: Favored\u2014municipal elections, public consultation, infrastructure projects, community safety responses, regional policy review.",
